{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["Who told you that you were naked? — the heh is an interrogative heh that stands (is read as part of the word)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "Rashbam identifies the grammatical form: the prefixed ה on המן is an interrogative particle joined to מן ('from'), yielding 'Who [told you] — from the tree?'; I render תמיהה המתקיימת as an interrogative that 'stands' i.e. is read together with the following word as one phonetic unit."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:44:15.717519493Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}